      ],
      "reason": "No model: the twin presents level 3 itself (4230 FEEDBACK section 2 m1). FAB-NOTES programs it by read-modify-write of OPTSR as read; the bench row reads bits 3:2 back as 11."
    },
    {
      "register": "GPIOA.AFRH",
      "class": "same-source",
      "fields": [
        "AFSEL9",
        "AFSEL10"
      ],
      "reason": "PA9/PA10 at AF7 for USART1: Renode's USART has no pin (4300b FEEDBACK section 0), so no AF choice shows in the twin. The bench row reads AFRH back after boot."
    },
    {
      "register": "GPIOA.AFRL",
      "class": "same-source",
      "fields": [
        "AFSEL5",
        "AFSEL6",
        "AFSEL7"
      ],
      "reason": "PA5-PA7 at AF5 for SPI1: the model routes a pin by AFR only for a timer channel (4300 FEEDBACK section 0). The bench row reads AFRL back; 3302 B2 predicted 0x555 there."
    },
    {
      "register": "GPIOA.MODER",
      "class": "same-source",
      "fields": [
        "MODER0",
        "MODER5",
        "MODER6",
        "MODER7",
        "MODER9",
        "MODER10"
      ],
      "reason": "PA0 output (flash CS), PA5-PA7 and PA9/PA10 alternate: a BSRR write drives a pin whatever MODER says (4200 FEEDBACK). The bench row reads MODER back, as 3302 B2 did."
    },
    {
      "register": "GPIOA.OSPEEDR",
      "class": "same-source",
      "fields": [
        "OSPEED0",
        "OSPEED5",
        "OSPEED6",
        "OSPEED7",
        "OSPEED9",
        "OSPEED10"
      ],
      "reason": "No edge rate is modelled; check speeds judges each chosen speed's fmax with svd-hal's own table, not an ir rule. The bench row reads OSPEEDR back."
    },
    {
      "register": "GPIOA.OTYPER",
      "class": "ignored-by-model",
      "fields": [
        "OT0",
        "OT1",
